sections.text:
Pains suddenly shift to different parts;
appear in remote localities^ as fingers and toes. Rum-
bling, with emission of much flatus. Griping, cutting in
hypogastric region, with intermittent cutting in stomach
and small intestines. Colic ; better walking about ;
pains radiate from abdomen to back, chest, arms;
worse, bending forwards and while lying. Gallstone
colic. Sharp pains from liver, shooting upivard to rigfit
nipple. Pain from gall-bladder to chest, back, and
arms. Renal colic, with pain in extremities.

Antidotes : Chamom. ; Camph.
Compare: Colocy. (differs in modalities); Nux;
Cham., Bry.
